  "structuring": {
    "prompt_additions": "In Tunisian legislation, ARTICLE is always the basic unit. SECTION, CHAPTER (CHAPITRE), and TITLE (TITRE) are higher divisions that contain articles, not the basic unit. Never treat SECTION as the basic unit. The first article is always 'Article premier' — normalise to ARTICLE 1. Alinéas (sub-paragraphs within articles) are unnumbered; use PARAGRAPH as the closest Bluebell keyword. French text is informative; Arabic text is authoritative."
  },
